config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a change of a template reaches the repositories
    accDescr: A pull request in this repository changes templates/ or the reusable workflows. Its checks lint them and check the set-up with the templates installed, while the required check issue-assistant compares this repository's own workflows with the release that they pin, so it stays green. Merged, the change becomes a release. A pull request in the repository blueprint installs that release there and moves the pins of the issue assistant. The next release of the blueprint brings it to every repository made from it, this one too. Repositories without the blueprint get the release from Dependabot or Renovate, which move the pins; they run install again only when the release changed a template.

    change["Pull request here<br>changes templates/<br>or the reusable workflows"]
    checks["Its checks pass<br>templates linted and installed<br>own workflows: the pinned release"]
    release["`Release **vX.Y.Z**<br>its notes name a changed template`"]
    sync["Pull request in the blueprint<br>install of vX.Y.Z<br>new pins of the issue assistant"]
    rollout(["Blueprint bot<br>an update pull request<br>in every repository of the blueprint"])
    fleet["Every repository of the blueprint<br>this one too<br>the jobs of vX.Y.Z"]
    others["Repositories without the blueprint<br>Dependabot or Renovate moves the pins<br>install again only for a changed template"]

    change --> checks --> release
    release --> sync --> rollout --> fleet
    release --> others

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class sync,rollout bot
    class change,others person
    class fleet done
